    "text": "2 days ago\nSpaceX’s IPO is set to be enormous — but it might not be this year’s biggest capital raise\nSpaceX's IPO comes as the company looks to raise more cash for its capital-intensive space and AI businesses. But tech giants and private AI companies are also hungry for more funding.\nLast week, Alphabet announced a $85 billion equity raise to support its AI buildout, which would top SpaceX's $75 billion base offering. However, if SpaceX's underwriters exercise the greenshoe offering for an additional $11.25 billion, the company could raise up to $86.25 billion.",
